WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:11.844
Long ago a boy named Jack lived with his mother.

2
00:00:13.105 --> 00:00:14.206
They were very poor.

3
00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:18.510
Jack's mother worked hard, but Jack was lazy.

4
00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:22.673
He spent his days playing and singing silly songs.

5
00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:26.877
Sometimes he stared at a castle in the distance.

6
00:00:26.897 --> 00:00:30.720
"I wonder who lives there," he thought.

7
00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:36.254
As he grew older, his mother grew impatient.

8
00:00:36.274 --> 00:00:40.496
"You need to find work," she said.

9
00:00:40.516 --> 00:00:43.738
"I will do my best, Mother!"

10
00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:44.979
Jack promised.

11
00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:49.161
Jack was not very bright, but he was kind.

12
00:00:52.363 --> 00:00:53.844
He soon found work at a mill.

13
00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:01.388
He worked hard, and the miller paid him a silver coin.

14
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:08.043
On his way home, Jack crossed a stream, and—splash!

15
00:01:09.104 --> 00:01:10.204
He dropped the coin.

16
00:01:16.128 --> 00:01:18.570
When Jack returned home, his mother moaned.

17
00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.632
"Oh, you silly boy!

18
00:01:21.652 --> 00:01:24.374
You must put your pay in your pocket."

19
00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:28.357
"I will do that," Jack said.

20
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.053
Next Jack found work at a bakery.

21
00:01:35.474 --> 00:01:37.235
The baker paid him with a loaf of bread.

22
00:01:39.316 --> 00:01:41.277
Jack stuffed the bread into his pocket.

23
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.081
I put my pay in my pocket!"

24
00:01:49.422 --> 00:01:50.502
Jack pulled out the bread.

25
00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:53.344
Crumbs spilled everywhere.

26
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:56.766
"Oh, you silly boy!

27
00:01:56.786 --> 00:01:59.407
You must carry your pay on your head!"

28
00:02:04.653 --> 00:02:06.653
Next Jack worked on a farm.

29
00:02:08.074 --> 00:02:10.054
His pay was a large jar of milk.

30
00:02:10.074 --> 00:02:14.215
"I must carry this jar on my head," Jack thought.

31
00:02:15.616 --> 00:02:17.656
Jack carefully put the jar on his head.

32
00:02:19.677 --> 00:02:21.657
But on his way home, it fell off.

33
00:02:22.078 --> 00:02:26.119
Crash! Mother sighed.

34
00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:30.160
"Oh, you silly boy!

35
00:02:30.656 --> 00:02:33.198
You must carry your pay on your shoulders."

36
00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:40.584
Next Jack worked at the market.

37
00:02:48.851 --> 00:02:51.092
work hard, Jack," his boss said.

38
00:02:51.112 --> 00:02:54.235
"I will pay you with this donkey."

39
00:02:56.537 --> 00:03:00.160
"I must put my pay on my shoulders," Jack thought.

40
00:03:01.376 --> 00:03:03.098
Jack put the donkey on his shoulders.

41
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.342
As he walked, he wobbled this way and that way.

42
00:03:08.362 --> 00:03:13.086
"This donkey is very heavy!"

43
00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:14.207
Jack thought.

44
00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.669
"I'll sing a silly song.

45
00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.192
That will make the trip easier."

46
00:03:19.212 --> 00:03:23.896
"Doodle-dee-doo! Doodle-dee-doo!"

47
00:03:23.916 --> 00:03:28.420
"Hee-haw!" The donkey seemed to sing along.

48
00:03:30.096 --> 00:03:32.438
Jack tried hard not to drop the donkey.

49
00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:37.783
So he didn't see the king and the princess pass by.

50
00:03:37.923 --> 00:03:40.045
The princess saw Jack zigzagging.

51
00:03:41.706 --> 00:03:44.208
She heard the funny song and burst into laughter.

52
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.051
The king's eyes lit up.

53
00:03:49.773 --> 00:03:52.615
The princess stopped smiling after her mother died.

54
00:03:55.218 --> 00:03:57.319
Now she couldn't stop laughing.

55
00:03:58.644 --> 00:04:00.686
"You!" the king yelled to Jack.

56
00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.688
"Come and meet the princess!"

57
00:04:06.591 --> 00:04:09.093
Soon Jack was a regular visitor at the castle.

58
00:04:10.514 --> 00:04:12.376
He and the princess laughed and sang.

59
00:04:12.396 --> 00:04:16.139
"Doodle-dee-doo! Doodle-dee-doo!"

60
00:04:16.159 --> 00:04:20.342
Later, of course, they got married, and lived very happily ever after.
